<#entry-task-03-decision-01> a schema:Comment;
    dct:created "2026-10-24T22:27:39Z"^^xsd:dateTime;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    schema:text "The multi-line editor does not become a combobox — the popup is exposed through a pattern researched against the WAI-ARIA APG, ProseMirror, Lexical and Tiptap-based apps; the concrete pattern is chosen after reviewing docs/research/mention-suggestion-accessibility.md.".
<#entry-task-03-openQuestion-01> a schema:Comment;
    dct:created "2026-10-24T22:27:39Z"^^xsd:dateTime;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    schema:text "Which pattern fits PodOS: the Lexical-style textbox plus aria-activedescendant, the Novel-style hidden-input combobox shim, or something else — per the research's trade-offs, and whether a live region should announce suggestion counts.".
<http://localhost:3000/dev/plans/mention-create-on-the-fly/plan.ttl#entry-task-03-scope-01> schema:text "The research note docs/research/mention-suggestion-accessibility.md establishes: no APG pattern exists for autocomplete inside a multi-line editor; Lexical sets aria-activedescendant and aria-controls on the editor root with a listbox popup and stable option ids, no combobox role; Novel shims a full combobox on a hidden input; ARIA 1.2 permits aria-activedescendant on role=textbox; aria-expanded is not valid on textbox in ARIA 1.2. Implementation follows the chosen pattern: option ids, editor-to-popup references, cleanup on onExit.".
